# .dockerignore — keep the build context small and keep user data OUT of image layers.
# `#` comments are supported; `!` negates.

.git
.gitignore
.cache
.pi
.vscode
.idea
*.log
*.md
!README.md
docs/
data/
cache/
tmp/
bin/
dist/
out/
.env
.env.*
node_modules/
__pycache__/
.venv/
coverage/
vendor/

# NOTE: *_test.go is deliberately NOT ignored. Excluding test files makes
# `go test ./...` (or any in-container test run) find zero tests and PASS
# VACUOUSLY — a false green that looks like coverage and proves nothing.
# If you must shrink the context, exclude build artifacts, never tests.

# NOTE: if this project bind-mounts a data/library folder (e.g. ./work, ./storage,
# ./media) instead of a named volume, ADD IT HERE. Otherwise the entire user data
# set is uploaded into the build context on every build and baked into image
# layers — slow builds and a leaky image.
